			<item>
				<title>Magnet is Damaged</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/macos_magnet_is_damaged/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 14 Jul 2023 22:16:55 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/macos_magnet_is_damaged/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;magnet-is-damaged&#34;&gt;Magnet is Damaged&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://magnet.crowdcafe.com&#34;&gt;Magnet&lt;/a&gt; is a nifty little app that allows Mac users to use Windows-style window snapping&lt;sup id=&#34;fnref:1&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#fn:1&#34; class=&#34;footnote-ref&#34; role=&#34;doc-noteref&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But: I installed Magnet from the App Store, and I&amp;rsquo;m running a current Mac and the latest macOS – how can an app get &lt;em&gt;damaged&lt;/em&gt; so that the only way to fix it is to reinstall it? I certainly never had any issue like this on an iPhone.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If Apple knows exactly how to fix it and Apple runs the App Store – why don&amp;rsquo;t they simply reinstall it? I mean isn&amp;rsquo;t an automatic app update more or less the same?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Apple&#39;s Privileges</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_4/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 30 May 2023 08:21:00 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_4/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;apples-privileges&#34;&gt;Apple&amp;rsquo;s Privileges&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since iOS and the App Store are Apple&amp;rsquo;s own platforms it gets special privileges and doesn&amp;rsquo;t have to follow its own rules.&#xA;Ever seen any third-party app getting such a nice screen asking for permissions?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And how about the dark pattern highlighting the &lt;em&gt;Enable Notifications&lt;/em&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Also: &lt;em&gt;Not Now&lt;/em&gt;? How about never?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apple/app_store_4.png&#34; alt=&#34;Apple asking for notifications permissions in the App Store.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Apple gets special treatment when asking for permissions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>App Store Dark Patterns</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_3/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 27 Apr 2023 08:55:00 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_3/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;services-are-apples-next-big-business&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Services&lt;/em&gt; are Apples Next Big Business&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;No, I didn&amp;rsquo;t want notifications the first time you asked. Or the second time. So no, I &lt;em&gt;still&lt;/em&gt; don&amp;rsquo;t want any notifications, even if you put them inline with the content.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apple/app_store_3.png&#34; alt=&#34;Apple asking for notifications in the App Store.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Apple sneakily trying to spam me.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>App Store Ads for Installed Apps</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_2/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 26 Mar 2023 14:37:00 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_2/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;apple-knows-how-to-make-the-app-store-a-premium-experience&#34;&gt;Apple Knows How to Make the App Store a Premium Experience&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, Apple is explicitly showing me something I&amp;rsquo;m &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; looking for.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Second, Apple knows Audible is already installed and decides to show me the ad anyway.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apple/app_store_2.png&#34; alt=&#34;Apple shows App Store ads for apps already installed on the device.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Apple Knows How to Make the App Store a Premium Experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>App Store Ads for the Top Result</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_1/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 05 Mar 2023 19:30:03 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/app_store_ads_1/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;ads-are-ruining-the-app-store&#34;&gt;Ads Are Ruining the App Store&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hey, wouldn&amp;rsquo;t it be cool if Apple didn&amp;rsquo;t show the app I&amp;rsquo;m searching for both as a giant ad and as a search result?&lt;sup id=&#34;fnref:1&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#fn:1&#34; class=&#34;footnote-ref&#34; role=&#34;doc-noteref&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apple/app_store_1.png&#34; alt=&#34;Ads are ruining Apple&amp;rsquo;s App Store.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ads are ruining Apple&amp;rsquo;s App Store.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;footnotes&#34; role=&#34;doc-endnotes&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li id=&#34;fn:1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I understand that Crunchy Bagel, the app developer, is not to blame. I genuinely adore &lt;a href=&#34;https://streaks.app&#34;&gt;Streaks&lt;/a&gt; and all of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://crunchybagel.com/about/&#34;&gt;other apps&lt;/a&gt; they offer. You should definitely check them out.&amp;#160;&lt;a href=&#34;#fnref:1&#34; class=&#34;footnote-backref&#34; role=&#34;doc-backlink&#34;&gt;&amp;#x21a9;&amp;#xfe0e;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>OpenVPN Dark Pattern</title>
				<link>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/open_vpn_rating/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 01 Dec 2022 08:57:00 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://s1999u2.github.io/annoyances/open_vpn_rating/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;openvpn-dark-pattern&#34;&gt;OpenVPN Dark Pattern&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Okay, so giving the OpenVPN app five stars takes me straight to the App Store. But for anything less, they want me to &amp;ldquo;take a survey&amp;rdquo; 🥵.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apps/open_vpn_5-stars.png&#34; alt=&#34;Giving the OpenVPN app five stars.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sure, rate the app.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://s1999u2.github.io/images/annoyances/apps/open_vpn_4-stars.png&#34; alt=&#34;Giving the OpenVPN app four stars.&#34;&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;No way, Jose, take a survey.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
			</item>
